{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a tracker, binds it to the current task with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length of its body, then finishes it and returns a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of every event tracked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through it. Each call makes its own tracker, so tests that run at once never see each other’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. Events tracked after the body returns, by work it started but didn’t wait for, are dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There are four spellings. The body can be synchronous or asynchronous, and it can take the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a parameter, for code that is handed its tracker (a SwiftUI view given it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker(_:)"},{"text":", a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"UIKit view controller given it as a trait) rather than reading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.current"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A recording holds what the body returned, every record with its timestamp, source location and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context, each event’s name, and the events of one type through "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording\/events(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to test targets 